    "text": "Let $f(z)=\\sum_{0\\leq k\\leq n} \\epsilon_k z^k$ be a random polynomial, where $\\epsilon_k\\in \\{-1,1\\}$ independently uniformly at random for $0\\leq k\\leq n$.\nIs it true that, if $R_n$ is the number of roots of $f(z)$ in $\\{ z\\in \\mathbb{C} : \\lvert z\\rvert \\leq 1\\}$, then $ \\frac{R_n}{n/2}\\to 1 $ almost surely?",
